  "_comment": "Claude Code model config for the orca app. Used by entrypoint.sh ONLY to seed a FRESH volume. An existing /home/orca/.claude/settings.json is never merged: it is authoritative and is kept in sync from the Windows PC by tools/sync-settings-to-orca.py. (A gap-fill merge here re-added absent keys on every boot and caused the 2026-10-18..2026-11-11 subagent-model bug.) This file only takes effect on a FRESH volume; the live volume keeps its own array. Mirrors the live volume file as of 2026-10-08 (23 picker rows); the two V4.1 Flash tier rows and the picker row moved to the `:1017-cloud` tag on 2026-10-17. Edit the volume file for runtime changes; edit this file only to change what a fresh volume gets. NOTE: each ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_*_MODEL_NAME must equal its ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_*_MODEL, or the picker shows one name and runs another model. CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL is deliberately ABSENT: when unset, subagents inherit the main session model. Do not add it back. entrypoint.sh deletes this key from settings.json on every boot.",
